# The build context is sent to the daemon in full before anything runs, so
# anything here that is not COPYed is pure latency on every build. Both images
# build from this directory (images/pipeline.Dockerfile, images/trigger.Dockerfile),
# so one ignore file serves both.
#
# This file is latency, not safety: what actually lands in an image is decided
# by the COPY lines, and tests/test_images.py is what holds those narrow.

.venv/
.venv-dashboard/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The student's own configuration, and both CAs. Neither image COPYs a
# certificate: the pipeline's TaskManager mounts the OpenSearch CA from a
# Kubernetes Secret, and the broker CA reaches Docling base64-encoded in the
# subscription. So none of it belongs in a build context, let alone a layer.
lab.yaml
certs/

# Everything neither image COPYs.
tests/
docs/
lab-documents/
scripts/
assets/
bootstrap.sh
setup.sh
pipeline.sh
*.md
.streamlit/
